DysruptionHub reports: A cyberattack forced Salida School District in Colorado to shut down its network June 29, damaging locally stored files and disrupting administrative operations, the district said. The attack began about 6:30 a.m. and was detected two hours later, according to a July 2 district notice. Officials took all systems offline and brought in specialists...
<p><a href="https://databreaches.net/2026/09/09/co-cyberattack-damages-files-at-salida-school-district-in-colorado/">Source</a></p>

